{"source_sentence": "Because the factory upgraded its filters last year, emissions in the surrounding valley have fallen sharply since then.", "correct_answer": "The air in that area has become considerably cleaner as a result of equipment the plant installed twelve months ago.", "distractors": [{"text": "The factory installed new filters because pollution in the surrounding area had already begun to drop.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The plant is scheduled to upgrade its filtering equipment next year, which should reduce local pollution.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Residents of the area pressured the plant into cutting the pollution it had produced for years.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "The source says the upgrade came first and caused the drop. The first wrong option reverses that order, making the drop the reason for the upgrade. The second moves the upgrade into the future when it has already happened. The third makes residents the cause, which the source never mentions.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"source_sentence": "Unless the museum secures additional funding, it will be forced to close its two smallest galleries by December.", "correct_answer": "Shutting the pair of minor exhibition rooms before the end of the year can only be avoided if more money is found.", "distractors": [{"text": "The museum will close its two smallest galleries by December, even if it secures additional funding.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The museum closed its two smallest galleries in December after failing to raise enough money.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Donors have decided to withdraw support for the museum's two smallest galleries before December.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "The source makes the closure conditional on funding not arriving. The first wrong option removes the condition, making closure happen regardless. The second reports the closure as already complete. The third turns the museum into the object of a donor decision, when the source only describes what the museum itself will be forced to do.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"source_sentence": "The council approved the housing plan only after developers agreed to fund a new access road.", "correct_answer": "Approval for the residential scheme depended on the builders committing to pay for additional infrastructure.", "distractors": [{"text": "Developers agreed to fund a new access road only after the council had approved the housing plan.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The council agreed to pay for a new access road so that developers would approve the housing plan.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The council is expected to approve the housing plan once developers begin building the access road.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "In the source the developers' commitment came first and made approval possible. The first wrong option puts approval first, reversing what depended on what. The second swaps who pays and who approves. The third presents the approval as still pending when the source says it has happened.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"source_sentence": "Although sales rose sharply in the final quarter, the company still ended the year with a loss.", "correct_answer": "A strong closing three months were not enough to prevent the firm finishing twelve months in deficit.", "distractors": [{"text": "Because sales rose sharply in the final quarter, the company managed to end the year profitably.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Sales are expected to rise sharply next quarter, which should move the company out of loss.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "The company's competitors saw sales rise sharply in the final quarter while it recorded a loss.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "The source concedes a good quarter but reports a bad year. The first wrong option turns the concession into a cause and the loss into a profit. The second moves the rise into the future. The third attributes the rise to competitors rather than to the company itself.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"source_sentence": "Residents were warned that the bridge would remain closed until engineers completed a full structural survey.", "correct_answer": "The crossing will not reopen before specialists have finished checking whether it is sound.", "distractors": [{"text": "The bridge reopened as soon as engineers had begun their structural survey.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Engineers will carry out a structural survey only after the bridge has been reopened to traffic.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Residents demanded that engineers close the bridge until a full structural survey was carried out.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "The source makes reopening wait for a completed survey. The first wrong option has the bridge open when the survey merely started. The second puts the survey after reopening, reversing the dependency. The third makes residents the ones demanding closure, when they were only warned of it.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"source_sentence": "The policy succeeded in rural districts but had almost no measurable effect in the larger cities.", "correct_answer": "What worked in the countryside made hardly any difference in major urban centres.", "distractors": [{"text": "The policy worked well in the largest cities but achieved little in rural districts.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "Rural districts adopted the policy while the larger cities rejected it outright.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "The policy is expected to succeed in rural districts before it reaches the larger cities.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The source pairs rural success with urban ineffectiveness. The first wrong option swaps which side each outcome belongs to. The second replaces a difference in effect with a difference in whether the policy was adopted at all. The third turns a reported result into a forecast.", "difficulty_est": 3}
{"source_sentence": "Unless attendance improves substantially over the summer, the festival organisers say that next year's event may be cancelled.", "correct_answer": "Scrapping the following year's gathering can be avoided only by a marked rise in visitor numbers.", "distractors": [{"text": "The festival will be cancelled next year even if attendance improves substantially over the summer.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The organisers cancelled this year's festival after attendance failed to improve over the summer.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}, {"text": "Visitors have told the organisers that they will not attend next year's festival unless it improves.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}], "explanation": "The source makes cancellation conditional on attendance staying low. The first wrong option removes the condition so cancellation happens regardless. The second reports a cancellation that has already occurred. The third swaps who is issuing the warning, making visitors rather than organisers the ones setting a condition.", "difficulty_est": 4}
{"source_sentence": "The law was intended to protect tenants, but landlords found several ways to work around it.", "correct_answer": "Although drafted to shield renters, the legislation left property owners with a number of loopholes.", "distractors": [{"text": "The law was intended to protect landlords, but tenants found several ways to work around it.", "distractor_type": "agent_swap"}, {"text": "Because landlords found ways around the law, it was later rewritten to protect tenants.", "distractor_type": "logic_flip"}, {"text": "The law will be introduced to protect tenants, though landlords are already preparing ways around it.", "distractor_type": "timing_shift"}], "explanation": "The source names tenants as the intended beneficiaries and landlords as the ones evading. The first wrong option swaps those two roles. The second makes the evasion the reason the law exists rather than a response to it. The third presents the law as not yet in force.", "difficulty_est": 3}
